Challenge: StegoRSA - picoCTF (Cryptography - Easy)

Files given:
- image.jpg (photo of a key)
- flag.enc (RSA encrypted flag)

Step 1: Ran exiftool on image.jpg
Command: exiftool image.jpg
Finding: Found a large hex string hidden in the Comment metadata field

Step 2: Decoded the hex string using Python
Command: python3 -c "print(bytes.fromhex('HEX').decode())" > private_key.pem
Finding: Hex decoded to a full RSA private key (-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----)

Step 3: Decrypted the flag using OpenSSL
Command: openssl rsautl -decrypt -inkey private_key.pem -in flag.enc
Result: Flag found successfully

Key Lessons:
- Always check file metadata with exiftool, not just the visible content
- Steganography hides data where people don't look
- RSA = two keys, public key locks, private key unlocks
- Hex is just another way to encode text/data
